      "name": "Jack Holloway",
      "role": "sheriff",
      "persona": "Tired lawman who has buried more men than he arrested. He wants the payroll found before a posse turns into a mob.",
      "knowledge": [
        "The stagecoach reached Dry Creek empty; the strongbox lid was pried, not shot open.",
        "The driver swears he never stopped between the mesa and town.",
        "Mabel Pruitt sold a new lock and a crowbar to a stranger two days back."
      ],
      "secrets": [
        "Jack lent the bank his own savings last spring and will be ruined if the payroll stays lost."
